    "q-142506": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142506",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider a sample of size $n=225$ from a population. Given that the sample mean is $98,$ and the sample standard deviation is $30,$ find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T>2.598)=0.005,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $224$ degrees of freedom.*",
      "worked_solution": "We do not know the distribution of the population, nor do we know the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ However, the sample size $n=225\\ge 30$ is *sufficiently large*.\n\nIn cases like this, the random variable\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{S/\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\ncan be approximated by the student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{n-1}$ with $n-1$ degrees of freedom, where\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${S}^{2}$ is the sample variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(T>{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ and $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1$ degrees of freedom.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=98,\\,n=225,\\,s=30.\n$$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $99%$ confidence interval. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.99=0.01\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.005.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>2.598)=0.005.$ As a result,\n\n$$\n{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}={t}_{224,0.005}=2.598.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14188481/assets/2b711e6fe35f64d886472fa38c5a65afd7473b344949d7effd49405946f3cee5.png)\n\nTherefore, the $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}98 & \\pm 2.598\\cdot \\frac{30}{\\sqrt{225}} \\\\ 98 & \\pm 5.196\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
